  <ym-title|Chapter 13: continuum correlations and local
  fields><label|chapter-13-continuum-correlations-and-local-fields>

  Read Scott/part2/F-infinite-volume.tex in full. Compared
  Martin/existence/limits.tex initial extraction assumptions and
  phase-fields.tex133\U240 for inclusion quantifiers. Scott's later full-UV
  formulation is used instead of Martin limits.tex's initial mesh-subsequence
  formulation: no new mesh extraction for observable kernels.

  <section|Sources and scope><label|sources-and-scope>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Volume extraction: Scott lem:F1, standard Arzela\UAscoli cited to
    Rudin1976 Theorem7.25. Compact exhaustions/basis labels/derivative orders
    form a countable family; all tests follow by integration.

    <item>Distinct-cell placement and vanishing errors: Scott
    lem:F-cells/F1b; the geometric strip count is retained, with the exact
    cell-margin hypothesis explicit. Uses the original FILS1978 chessboard
    theorem previously inspected by root, not a new independent reflection
    proof.

    <item>Null fields and rank: Scott lem:F2. Three precise inputs isolate
    bounded transported null directions, upper projector rank, and actual
    interacting/free detector matrices. Both rank inequalities included; free
    positivity alone not promoted to interacting rank.

    <item>Simultaneous representative: Scott lem:F-represent. Normalization
    b=(1+\|\|Pi x\|\|)^-1 and compact pair (b,bPi x) handles unbounded
    approximate labels. Its normalized null hypothesis is explicitly stronger
    than the bounded-family null condition. Ordered-filter compactness does
    not alter the full UV kernel limit.

    <item>Inclusions/derivatives: Scott F2 and Martin phase-fields133ff.
    Representatives chosen before all spectators/tests, then basiswise linear
    maps. Torus summation-by-parts sign checked. Quotient
    coherence/commutation follows from all-spectator nullity.

    <item>Reflection and polynomial bounds: Scott F3. Moving bond plane tends
    to zero, tests stay separated. Full O(4) and collision extension
    deferred. Scale thickness a_next\<gtr\>=c a\<twosuperior\> gives
    two-stage r^4 cell lower bound.

    <item>Repeated words: Scott F4. At most2n residues regardless of
    repetitions, main scale chosen before exterior, aligned finer exterior
    tiling, constant B_v independentj, cutoff thresholds alloweddependj. No
    bounded Hilbert operator presupposed.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Retained analytic inputs><label|retained-analytic-inputs>

  Chapter12 full-UV and volume-uniform difference hypotheses remain the
  inherited scope until Chapter11 suppliers close. Corrected equation-null,
  inclusion/derivative estimates for subpower-growing coefficients, actual
  finite-detector rank comparison, centered seminorm bounds and interior-cell
  comparisons are explicitly inputs. Their detailed realization belongs
  Chapter11; Chapter13 proves their continuum consequences without claiming
  they follow from compactness.

  Independent review requested. Global root build and rendered review pending
  final integration.
